KZ2 patch 6064: LD_CB_REUSE, reuse the previous draw's vertex constant-buffer slot. Default off.

From Killzone 3 port patch 2148 (KZ3 an earlier change; the Killzone 3 PC port "Project Helghast", same author, MIT; read at Project Helghast
port/patches/2148-live-draw-constant-buffer-reuse.patch, snapshot work/kz3-import/2026-11-04-walker). Default off, as in KZ3.

Every live draw copies the 512 transform constants plus an 8-float tail (viewport transform) into a slot of the constant
ring (8 KB of write-combined memory per draw). With LD_CB_REUSE=1 a draw whose constants are unchanged since the draw that
filled the previous slot, and whose tail bytes are equal, points its root CBV at that slot and skips the copy; the ring
does not advance for it. "Unchanged" is a generation counter (rsx_dispatch.const_gen) bumped by every writer of the
stored constants when a value changes: the transform-constant upload in rsx_dispatch.c, the constant seed, and the camera
repair in rsx_live_draw.c (KZ2's tree has no other writer of g.rsx.constants; checked by grep in an earlier change). The
previous slot must also lie below the ring's write position, and every ring reset (the five cb_used = 0 sites in KZ2's
rsx_live_draw.c) invalidates it. The decision is in rsx_cb_reuse.h (pure functions), tested by
tools/runtime/test_walker73.sh. With RSX_PERF=1 the [perf-walk] line ends with "| cbv copy N reuse M".

